to very high standards. That's
how I've achieved what I have today.

144
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:02,870
I want to look perfect on camera,

145
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:05,190
without a single flaw—

146
00:11:06,270 --> 00:11:07,440
not even on my body.

147
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:10,460
What exactly are you suggesting?

148
00:11:11,390 --> 00:11:12,320
I want a new face.

149
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:14,400
I want a full-face skin graft.

150
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,730
A full-face skin graft?

151
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:16,840
That procedure

152
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:18,840
is still in the experimental stage.

153
00:11:19,230 --> 00:11:20,750
It's not only extremely expensive,

154
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:21,750
but we'd also need

155
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:24,270
to find a donor whose face
is a perfect match for yours.

156
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:26,030
We might not find

157
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:28,480
even one suitable donor
among ten thousand people.

158
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,090
And even if I could guarantee

159
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:32,000
the success of your procedure,

160
00:11:32,470 --> 00:11:33,150
the donor

161
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,340
would

162
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:39,640
be left severely disfigured.

163
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,390
All I need from you

164
00:11:41,390 --> 00:11:43,500
is the criteria for a suitable donor.

165
00:11:44,030 --> 00:11:46,230
Whether that person ends up disfigured

166
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,930
is none of your concern.

167
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:51,970
I just want my face restored
to its original condition,

168
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,320
or even better than before.

169
00:12:05,190 --> 00:12:08,390
I can make the decision
to undergo a full-face skin graft.

170
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:11,440
I'm willing to have someone else's face
ripped off

171
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,140
and grafted onto mine.

172
00:12:14,910 --> 00:12:17,320
I won't let anyone stand in my way—

173
00:12:17,790 --> 00:12:18,720
not even

174
00:12:19,390 --> 00:12:20,150
Lin Di'er.

175
00:12:21,390 --> 00:12:23,910
You lecture me
about knowing where to draw the line?

176
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:25,510
I've seen what kind of person
you are, Chen Jihong,

177
00:12:25,510 --> 00:12:27,120
since I was a child.

178
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,000
I should thank my dear mother.

179
00:12:31,910 --> 00:12:34,000
You should praise me, Mom.

180
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,510
I've outdone my own mother.

181
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,030
Xiao,

182
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:43,000
